  "worked_solution": "The area of the square is given by \n\n$$\nA=A(l)={l}^{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length of the side of the square.\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(l)$ with respect to $l$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{\u2032}(l) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}l}({l}^{2})=2l.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
